A||||17||LT1 Chop Top||Chunks of 'stuff' in my exhaust pipe!!||||5||
Z||000000||LT1 Chop Top||12-22-2001||07:42 PM||||After I changed my oil on my 88 GT, i decided to 'adjust' the exhaust on the Supertrapps.  When I open one of the pipes it was cramed FULL of the pieces pictured below.  This was one of the larger pieces.  Is this from the catalitic converter??  I cleaned all 4 of the pipes out, and drove around for a while, and I gotta say..it sure drives better w/o plugged up pipes! If it is the cat...what do I need to do? <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/exhaust1.jpg">  <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/exhaust2.jpg">  <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/lt1choptopsig_1.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by LT1 Chop Top (edited 12-22-2001).]||||reg||5
Z||000001||avengador1||12-22-2001||07:50 PM||||It does look like a piece of ceramic core. You could take the cat off and finish cleaning it out, or put a high flow one on.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Avendgador1.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by avengador1 (edited 12-22-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Standard||12-22-2001||07:53 PM||||Yup, that's what the cat converter looks like inside.  I had a few chunks like that fall out when I took my cat off.  I say finish cleaning it out  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/quad_sig_pic_1.jpg">        <BR><FONT COLOR="red">1988 Quad 4 Coupe 5 speed</FONT><BR><FONT SIZE="1"><FONT COLOR="white">1986 GT 5 speed, 1984 SC Auto</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="blue">AOL: LastMinuteBastrd  AIM: SavedbyJebus</FONT></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000003||GT GT 87||12-22-2001||09:57 PM||||I recently had a 40% powerer loss in my '87 GT . I pulled the cat off , it was plugged up , and when I nocked it on the garage floor , many pieces like yours fell out . The exhaust note on your car (like mine)will be much louder when you get rid of the cat .||||reg||1
Z||000004||Dumba$$||12-22-2001||10:50 PM||||that isnt from a factory cat, so most likley that already was a (high flow cat)<BR>the factory cat has a baffle in the middle and on the top side of the baffle sits about 500-1000 little ceramic?  beads a little smaller than a pea are crammed in there  (very restrictive)<BR>imo <BR>dont gut it, it sounds much nicer if you can just replace it with a straight pipe (if you dont have emissions crap where u live)<BR>or get a new cat!! i think pretty much all cats are now concidered (high flow)as they are a much better design than they were in the mid 80's<BR>i have replaced my cats with straight pipe on my 86 and 84   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">me likes much better <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>just my .02 cents<P>------------------<BR>Rich<BR>Sioux Falls SD<BR>Red 84 SE<BR>Gold 86 SE <BR>98 acura cl 3.0<P>ever notice that people that own a fiero, either have, or have had other fieros?||||reg||1
Z||000005||Standard||12-22-2001||11:35 PM||||It'll definatly be louder if you replace it with a straight pipe.  A hollow cat acts like an expansion chamber.. tones the sound down a bit.  well, at least it did for my quad.  Definatly changed the sound when I went from a hollow cat to a straight pipe.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Archie||12-23-2001||12:08 AM||||When you had the Supertraps put on did you have new cats installed too?  If not then those units have been on the car for nearly what 4 years now? Time to replace them maybe. <P>I would either put on new cats or install some mufflers...... i don't think u want it too loud or you wouldn't have installed the supertraps.<P>Archie||||reg||1
Z||000007||LT1 Chop Top||12-23-2001||02:02 AM||||Archie,<P>The exhaust system came with the car when I bought it (2.5 years ago) so I have no idea of its total age.  Is there a way to clean it out w/o cutting the pipe?<P>What is the difference between a cat and a muffler??<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/lt1choptopsig_1.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000008||Standard||12-23-2001||02:38 AM||||A cat is filled with a ceramic element, like what you pulled out of your tips.  It's designed to 'clean up' the exhaust.  Get rid of emissions, burn any excess gas that's in the exhaust.  A muffler is essentially a chamber filled with a series of baffles, designed to just quite down the exhaust note.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Bruiser||12-23-2001||04:07 AM||||While on the subject of exhaust. Does anyone know if resonator tips on a 2M4 would be worth it? I dunno about Monza tips or anything, but theres some cheap rip offs at Canadian Tire for like $20US I might invest in.||||reg||6
Z||000010||Archie||12-23-2001||09:06 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by LT1 Chop Top:<BR><B>Archie,<P>The exhaust system came with the car when I bought it (2.5 years ago) so I have no idea of its total age.  Is there a way to clean it out w/o cutting the pipe?<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yes, that will make it about 4 years.<P>I have never "Gutted a Cat" so I don't know how you would clean it out without taking it apart. Maybe a "Roto-Rooter". I'm sure someone here knows how to gut it.<P>Archie<p>[This message has been edited by Archie (edited 12-23-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000011||4BanGinFun||12-23-2001||05:34 PM||||you can gut it with a long screw driver or a broom handle <P>it worked good for when i had to hollow out the cat on the ice racer at school <P>im not sure if this method will work on your cat worked good on a ford one.<P>------------------<BR>85 se 2m4 5spd white<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.stopstart.fsnet.co.uk/flags/canada.gif"> <BR>www.angelfire.com/super/camaro0/||||reg||1
Z||000012||Standard||12-23-2001||07:34 PM||||I just used a half-inch copper pipe I had laying around.  Anything you can stick in there to break up the element will work.. except you'll have to take the cat off the car first.||||reg||1
Z||000013||Fierokid87||12-23-2001||11:18 PM||||Im gonna be running a bran new rebuilt 2.9(2.8 30 over) and i was wondering if I would need the cat in the exaust?  I mean we have emissions.  But i always thought a new engine will run cleaner then an older engine.<P>Scott<P>------------------<BR><FONT COLOR="red"> Fierokid's  Web site:</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="white">http://www.angelfire.com/sports/sfiero</FONT><P><FONT COLOR="blue">AIM: Fierokid87<BR>ICQ: Fierokid</FONT><P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fierokid.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000014||turbo time||12-24-2001||09:52 AM||||Pick up a universal high flow cat from a performance shop, they're under $100 and can be welded on. It will make your car a lot quieter and in most cases (except turbos) give a bit more torque in your engine from the backpressure. I'm not a green freak but for $100 for a cat I'm all in for doing my part.||||reg||1
Z||000015||Formula88||12-24-2001||11:49 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Fierokid87:<BR><B>Im gonna be running a bran new rebuilt 2.9(2.8 30 over) and i was wondering if I would need the cat in the exaust?  I mean we have emissions.  But i always thought a new engine will run cleaner then an older engine.<P>Scott<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>If you have emissions testing, you will fail just on the visual inspection without a cat. ||||reg||1
Z||000016||Nashco||12-24-2001||02:39 PM||||I don't think you want to ream out the center of your cats, especially with those supertrapps.  If you ram the centers out, the outer edges will still want to break apart and come rattling through your exhuast and sit up against the supertrapps.  Look how much money is invested in this car, is a couple hundred bucks on a cat. con. that big of a deal???  Not only will it be cleaner, but the exhaust will also be a little smoother sounding.<P>Just my $.02, take what you will from it.<P>------------------<BR>Bryce<BR> <IMG SRC="http://home1.gte.net/jbnash/nashcosig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000017||LT1 Chop Top||12-24-2001||04:48 PM||||Is there a problem after all the crud comes out of the cat, if I don't do anything??  Will the exhaust flow more freeley then??<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/lt1choptopsig_1.gif"> ||||reg||1
